# Redirect rules, applied by the host before its own 404 fallback.
#
# Syntax (Netlify/Cloudflare):  <from-path>  <to-path>  <status>
#   301 = permanent (use for renamed / migrated URLs)
#   302 = temporary
#   Trailing slashes match Astro's `trailingSlash: 'always'` — keep them on both sides.
#   ALWAYS include a no-slash variant for each rule. Matching is
#   exact; Astro's trailingSlash: 'always' only normalizes paths that
#   exist in dist/, so /foo (no slash) 404s unless we list it explicitly.
#   Wildcards: `/old/*  /new/:splat  301` forwards the matched suffix.
#
# Organize new entries under the matching section below. If none of the
# sections fit, add a new one with a heading comment.

